    "notes": "# Colemak + HandsDown · Corne v4.1\n\nGenerated by `users/raphaelmor/tools/kle_export.py` from the QMK sources.\nDo not hand-edit — regenerate instead.\n\n## Reaching a layer\n\nEach layer's picture marks the key you **hold** to get there in red. Where the two\nbases differ the column reads Colemak / HandsDown.\n\n```\n  layer  hold   position\n  ----------------------\n  Media  Esc    LH2\n  Nav    ␣      LH1\n  Mouse  Tab    LH0\n  Sym    ⏎ / R  RH0\n  Num    ⌫      RH1\n  Fun    ⌦ / ⏎  RH2\n```\n\n## Combos — 18\n\nA combo is a set of key *positions*, not of letters. Most are limited to\nthe HandsDown base, but 3 are not, so those also fire on\nColemak — at whatever letters sit under those positions.\n\n```\n  Colemak  HandsDown  sends                                            positions\n  --------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n  S+T      T+H        th                                               LM2+LM1\n  W+P      W+M        qu — hold past 200 ms to drop the u and leave q  LT3+LT1\n  R+T      N+H        Z                                                LM3+LM1\n\n  HandsDown base only\n           A+E        acute dead key (⌥E) — é                          RM1+RM2\n           E+I        grave dead key (⌥`) — è                          RM2+RM3\n           A+I        circumflex dead key (⌥I) — ê                     RM1+RM3\n           U+O        umlaut dead key (⌥U) — ü                         RB1+RB2\n           V+J        tilde dead key (⌥N) — ñ                          LT4+LT0\n           S+T        ç (⌥C)                                           LM4+LM2\n           E+O        œ (⌥Q)                                           RM2+RB2\n           A+U        æ (⌥')                                           RM1+RB1\n           V+W+G      Shift-Tab                                        LT4+LT3+LT2\n           M+J        App menu                                         LT1+LT0\n           ,+A        ;                                                RM0+RM1\n           .+\"        :                                                RT1+RT3\n           /+\"        ?                                                RT2+RT3\n           .+/        !                                                RT1+RT2\n           Y+B        Caps Word on or off                              RB3+RB4\n```\n\n## Adaptive keys — 22\n\nOnly on the HandsDown base. Roll two keys inside 175 ms and the\nsecond one rewrites the pair. Rules that name three letters need the\nthird-from-last key too (only available on QMK on the Corne).\n\n```\n  P B D -> PWD                                         (fires on D after P+B)\n  W M G -> WML                                         (fires on G after W+M)\n  PD -> PWD (insert W, D continues)                    (fires on D after P)\n  PF -> PS                                             (fires on F after P)\n  KG -> KL                                             (fires on G after K)\n  MG -> LG (del M, L, G continues)                     (fires on G after M)\n  JG -> JPG (insert P, G continues)                    (fires on G after J)\n  WG -> WD                                             (fires on G after W)\n  KH -> KN                                             (fires on H after K)\n  GJ -> ...g + \"th\" (e.g. \"length\")                    (fires on J after G)\n  WJ -> WL                                             (fires on J after W)\n  MK -> LK (del M, L, K continues)                     (fires on K after M)\n  HK -> NK (del H, N, K continues)                     (fires on K after H)\n  GM -> GL                                             (fires on M after G)\n  VM -> VL                                             (fires on M after V)\n  FP -> SP (del F, S, P continues)                     (fires on P after F)\n  GV -> GT                                             (fires on V after G)\n  MV -> LV (del M, L, V continues)                     (fires on V after M)\n  GW -> GD                                             (fires on W after G)\n  MW -> MP                                             (fires on W after M)\n  YB -> IB (del Y, I, B continues)                     (fires on B after Y)\n  AE -> AU (keeps home row)                            (fires on E after A)\n```\n\n## Always on\n\n- **Linger brackets** — Tap ( or { for one bracket. Hold past 200 ms for the pair, caret inside: (|)  `ramo_linger.c:20`\n- **Caps Word** — Letters get ⇧. Digits, -, _, ⌫ keep it on. Space → _, double space → real space + off.  `ramo_linger.c:55`\n- **Shift + ⌫ = ⌦** — Keeps Delete reachable on Hands Down, where it left the thumb row.  `ramo_process_record.c:45`\n- **Comma-leader shift** — Hands Down only. Type , then a letter within 200 ms → the comma goes, the letter gets ⇧.  `ramo_process_record.c:60`\n- **Combo hold on qu** — Hold the W+M combo past 200 ms and the u is deleted, leaving q.  `ramo_combos.c:164`\n- **Base switch** — NAV layer, two left keys. Double-tap only, so a stray press cannot change your base.  `ramo_tap_dance.c:11`\n\n## Not drawn\n\nThe board has 46 switches. These 10 are left off:\n\n- Outer pinky column `LT5 LM5 LB5 RT5 RM5 RB5` — `KC_NO` on every layer.\n- Inner ex2 keys `LTA LMA RTA RMA`.\n\nCareful: these hidden positions do have something bound.\n\n- `CMK_LTA` is `LCTL_T(KC_A)`\n- `CMK_RTA` is `LCTL_T(KC_A)`\n- `CMK_LMA` is `LCTL_T(KC_A)`\n- `CMK_RMA` is `LCTL_T(KC_A)`",
    "plate": true
